 - **Backup of the open store.** ObjectBox's backup API is server-only and closing the store would invalidate every repository and cubit, so `backupOpenStore` (`migrations/backup.dart`) copies `data.mdb` inside a read transaction: the file is copy-on-write, so while a reader is open no writer reuses its snapshot's pages and the copy is one committed state. Same temporary-name-then-rename rule as the migration backup; the name is `data.mdb.pre-import-<UTC yyyyMMdd-HHmmss-SSS>`.
